Russia's Foreign Ministry claimed Monday that Estonia is "tacitly" allowing Ukraine to use its airspace to strike targets inside Russia.
Russia also repeated an earlier allegation and warning that such a move could lead to "open war" following a Russian cargo ship catching fire in Estonia's exclusive economic zone in the Gulf of Finland.
The ministry issued the statement after summoning Estonia's charg&eacute; d'affaires in Moscow, Marek &Uuml;htegi, to lodge a formal protest over Estonia's decision to close its land border with Russia and over Tallinn's accusations linking Russian military intelligence to an attempted arson attack on a defense facility near Tallinn.
